Carafe: the runtime's own DXVK is the system Direct3D. Its d3d8, d3d9, d3d10core, d3d11 and dxgi sit in
syswow64 and system32 in place of Wine's, which draw through OpenGL that the Switch does not give games, and
dxwrapper's ddraw sits in syswow64 in place of Wine's ddraw. A DXVK folder goes in front of system32 only when
it exists, so for that DXVK the search path is as on Windows: the game's folder first, then the system folder, and
a DLL loaded by its system path, as mod loaders do, is Carafe's too. A DXVK release installed beside it still
comes from its own folder, and VKD3D-Proton still comes from C:\vkd3d64.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

